  "job_B8.5.4.1_20251003_114912": {
    "text": "On Tiberius dagum \u00f0\u00e6s miclan caseres hyt gelamp bynnan lytlum fyrste, \u00e6fter\u00feam \u00fee ure heofenlica\nAnd he w\u00e6s on Equitania rice cyning under Tyberie \u00feam casere, and he w\u00e6s oftost wunigende on \u00fe\u00e6re\nAnd he w\u00e6s se ylca Tyrus, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e bec secga\u00f0, swa unhal on hys andwlitan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t adl, \u00fee we hata\u00f0\nAc hyt w\u00e6s \u00fea, \u00fe\u00e6t sum man w\u00e6s farende of Iudea lande.\n\u00de\u00e6s nama w\u00e6s Nathan and he w\u00e6s anes burhmannes sunu on Ysrahela lande, \u00fe\u00e6s nama w\u00e6s Nau.\nAc se ylca Nathan w\u00e6s swa gely\u00f0en, \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6fde gefaren fram \u00e6lcum lande to o\u00f0rum and fram s\u00e6 to\nAnd se ylca Nathan w\u00e6s \u00fea asend fram Tyberie \u00feam casere to Romes burh to \u00feam, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde hys\nAnd Nathan \u00fea w\u00e6s for\u00f0werd farende myd eallum hys \u00e6rende toweard Romana rice, and \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s on\nAc se su\u00f0erna wynd hyne and hys anf\u00e6reld \u00fea swy\u00f0e gedrehte and hyne swa genydde, \u00fe\u00e6t he to \u00feam\nAnd Tyrus \u00fea \u00f0\u00e6re burge hlaford wear\u00f0 \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t geseonde and sona oncneow be heora f\u00e6relde, \u00fe\u00e6t hig\nAnd he sona \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0 and w\u00e6s swy\u00fee wundrigende: N\u00e6fre ic \u00e6r on \u00feyssum lande swylc wundor ne\nAc Tyrus \u00fea het \u00fe\u00e6rto yrnan and hym to clypian \u00feone \u00fee on \u00feam scype yldost w\u00e6re.\nAnd Nathan hym sona to com.\nAnd Tyrus hyne sona axode and hym to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t eart \u00feu to so\u00f0e o\u00f0\u00f0e hwanon come \u00feu?\nNathan hym andswarode \u00fea and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic eom Nathan, Nauwes sunu, and ic of Greca rice hyder\nTyrus hym \u00fea andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: La, gif \u00feu myhtest \u00e6fre \u00e6nig \u00feing fyndan on smyrunge o\u00f0\u00f0e on\nNathan hym andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: Eala myn hlaford, ic ne m\u00e6g nane swylce \u00feyng fyndan, ne ic \u00fe\u00e6r\nAc gif \u00feu gefyrn on Iudea lande w\u00e6re, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00f0u myhtest fyndan swylcne man and acorenne wytegan, \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe sylf h\u00e6lde hys folc fram heora synnum and eac he myd hys worde hreoflan acl\u00e6nsode and he\nAnd sum wyf w\u00e6s \u00feoligende blodes fleusan huru XII wynter, seo w\u00e6s Veronix genemned, and heo\nAnd he of V hlafon and of twam fixum fif \u00feusend manna gefylde.\nEalle \u00feas \u00feyng and o\u00f0re f\u00e6la \u00e6r his \u00ferowunge he gefylde.\nAc \u00fea Iudeas w\u00e6ron myd andan afyllede and hyne gefengon and \u00fea ealdras and \u00fea m\u00e6ssepreostas hyne\nAnd hig hym dryncan sealdon, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s wyn and eced gemenged tog\u00e6dere, and he eac on \u00fe\u00e6re rode\nAnd Ioseph se ryhtwysa wer his lychaman bebyrigde.\nAnd \u00fea Iudeas \u00fe\u00e6rto hyrdas gesetton and \u00fe\u00e6rofer sceoldon wacian, \u00feyl\u00e6s hys cnyhtas comon and \u00fe\u00e6ne\nAc ic secge to so\u00f0on, \u00fe\u00e6t on \u00feam ylcan lychaman, \u00fee he myd bebyrged w\u00e6s, on \u00feam ylcan he eft aras\nTirus w\u00e6s \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t gehyrende eall swy\u00f0e georne and hys heafod up ahebbende and on Cryst gelyfende,\nAc \u00f0a \u00fea Tyrus h\u00e6fde \u00feus gespecen, hym \u00fea of \u00feam andwlytan ny\u00f0er afeoll se Cancer, \u00fee hyne \u00e6r\nAnd Tyrus \u00fea ny\u00f0er afeoll on eor\u00f0an astreht and hyne to dryhtne geb\u00e6d and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: La \u00e6lmyhtyga\nAc \u00e6fter\u00feam \u00fee he hyne \u00feus gebeden h\u00e6fde, he to hym Nathan geclypode and hym to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Eala, hu\nCum ra\u00f0e and fulla me, \u00fe\u00e6t ic m\u00e6ge myd ealre heortan on hyne gelyfan, for\u00feon ic hyne n\u00e6fre ne\nNathan hym \u00fea to geneal\u00e6hte and hyne sona gefullode on naman f\u00e6deres and suna and halgan gastes,\nAnd Tytus \u00fea asende bodan to hys fyrdgemacan, \u00fee w\u00e6s genemned Vespasianus, \u00fee w\u00e6s eac h\u00e6\u00f0en;\nAnd Vespasianus \u00fea butan \u00e6lcere yldynge hym ongean com myd seofen \u00feusend gew\u00e6pnodra manna.\nAnd \u00fea he on \u00fea ceastre becom Libie, he \u00fea sona axode, hw\u00e6t hyt so\u00f0es w\u00e6re, for hwig hym man swa\nTitus hym andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: Eala, for hwig ne besceawast \u00feu on \u00feynre heortan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u gelyfe on\nAc uton wyt nu beon hys leorningcnyhtas and faran and hyne gewrecan and ealle hys fynd adylgian of\nTitus and Vespasianus heora ge\u00feeaht h\u00e6fdon, swa \u00feeah \u00fe\u00e6t Vespasianus w\u00e6s \u00e6rost gefullod.\nAnd hig sy\u00f0\u00f0an of Libia \u00fe\u00e6re ceastre foron and on scyp astigon and to Hierusalem ferdon and hig eall\nAc \u00fea \u00f0a cyningas, \u00fee on \u00feam lande wunedon, \u00fe\u00e6t gehyrdon, hig w\u00e6ron swy\u00f0e gedrefede and to\nAnd se cyning Herodes \u00fea wear\u00f0 swa swy\u00f0e gedrefed, \u00fe\u00e6t he cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Archelause hys suna: La myn\nNu \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e we to so\u00f0on wyton, \u00fe\u00e6t se sylfa Herodes \u00fea hys spere genam and hyne sylfne ofstang and\nAnd Archelaus hys sunu \u00fea com to \u00feam o\u00f0rum cyningum, \u00fee w\u00e6ron ryxiende eond eall \u00fe\u00e6t Iudeisce\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6ron \u00e6rest of ehta ricum ehta cyningas myd eallum \u00feam folce, \u00fee heom myd woldon, and hig\nAc se wysdom weox myd Tite and myd Vespasiane, swa \u00fe\u00e6t hig h\u00e6fdon ealle \u00fea ricu eondfarene and\nAnd hyt w\u00e6s \u00fea on \u00feam ehto\u00f0an geare, \u00fee se mycla hungor heom on becom, \u00fe\u00e6t hig for \u00fe\u00e6re\nAc \u00fea yldestan cempan, \u00fea \u00f0e on Hierusalem w\u00e6ron and of \u00feam ehta ricon, heom betwynan\nSelre us ys to so\u00f0on, \u00fe\u00e6t we us sylfe ofslean, \u00feonne hig us yfelum dea\u00f0e acwylmon and eft secgon,\nAc ic wat, \u00fe\u00e6t hig heora swurd \u00fea abrudon and heom betweonan fuhton, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6r w\u00e6ron on d\u00e6g ealra\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t folc, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6r \u00e6fter on \u00fe\u00e6re ceastre belyfen w\u00e6s, \u00fea w\u00e6ron sume to dea\u00f0e af\u00e6rede for \u00fe\u00e6ra\nAc uton ure heafdo ahyldan and \u00feysse ceastre c\u00e6gean \u00feysum Romaniscan folce agyfan, for\u00feam \u00f0e we\nAc uton hig on hand syllan Tyte and Vespasiane and heom \u00feus to cwe\u00f0an: Her we sylla\u00f0 eow, urum\nAnd we \u00fe\u00e6t nu wyton, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0ys rice ys eower and na leng ure, and hyt ys eow geseald \u00feurh Messian,\nEall \u00fe\u00e6t folc heom \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t gecuron and \u00feam Romaniscan here on hand eodon and heom \u00feus to\nAc \u00fea \u00f0a hig \u00feus gesprecen h\u00e6fdon, hig w\u00e6ron sona on \u00e6lcere healfe gefangene and f\u00e6ste gewry\u00f0ene\nAnd Titus and Vespasianus \u00fea heom betwynan ge\u00feeaht worhton, swa \u00fe\u00e6t hig of \u00feam Iudeum, \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6r\nAnd hig w\u00e6ron \u00fea Titus and Vespasianus heom eall \u00fe\u00e6t Iudeisce land agende and georne ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd hyt swa \u00feeah swa gesmeadon, \u00fe\u00e6t hig an wyf fundon, \u00fe\u00e6re nama w\u00e6s Veronix, and heo w\u00e6s\nHeo w\u00e6s \u00fea sumne d\u00e6l h\u00e6bbende of \u00feam reafe \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes and hyt swy\u00f0e deorwyr\u00f0lice heold and\nAnd Titus and Vespasianus \u00fea hyre \u00e6fter asendon, and heo heom myd manega dagas wunede, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd hig sy\u00f0\u00f0an bodan asendon to Romes burh to \u00feam casere Tyberie to \u00feam, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde\nTiberius \u00fea se casere swa dyde and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Volosiane hys m\u00e6ge: Far and onfoh ealle \u00fea \u00f0ing, \u00fee \u00f0u\nAnd asend swylcne dom ofer \u00fea Iudeiscan cyningas, eall swylcne hig ofer \u00feone h\u00e6lend asendon, and\nAnd gif \u00feu \u00feone man to me gel\u00e6dest, \u00fee myne wunda geh\u00e6le, ic wylle on \u00feone h\u00e6lend godes sunu\nVolosianus hym andswarode and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Gea hlaford, and hw\u00e6t, gif ic swylcne man gemete,\nTiberius hym andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: Beo \u00feanon \u00fee he beo, sig he cynyng \u00e6fter me.\nVolosianus hym \u00fea w\u00e6s for\u00f0werdes farende and on anes d\u00e6ges f\u00e6relde to s\u00e6 becom; seo s\u00e6 hatte\nAnd he \u00fe\u00e6r on scyp eode and myd hys scypre\u00f0rum hys segl up ahof and swy\u00f0e for\u00f0 seglode, and swa\nAnd he sona hig ealle axode, hwylce d\u00e6da be \u00feam h\u00e6lende gedone w\u00e6ron.\n\u00d0a com Ioseph of Arimathia and Nychodemus myd hym and hym eall s\u00e6don, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t hig \u00fe\u00e6ron\nNichodemus s\u00e6de: Ic wat, \u00fe\u00e6t ic hyne geseah, and \u00fe\u00e6t ic wat fullgeorne, \u00fe\u00e6t he ys ealles\nIoseph hym \u00fea to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic wat, \u00fe\u00e6t ic hyne of \u00fe\u00e6re rode genam and hyne on \u00fea byrgene lede, \u00fee ic\nAc ic \u00fe\u00e6r twegen englas geseah, \u00e6nne \u00e6t \u00feam heafdon and o\u00f0erne \u00e6t \u00feam fotum, and eac hig me\nIc heom andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: \u00feone onhangenan h\u00e6lend ic sece.\nHig cw\u00e6don me ongean: Fara\u00f0 on Galileam, \u00fe\u00e6r ge magon hyne geseon, swa swa he eow \u00e6r\nAnd eac \u00e6fter \u00feysum cw\u00e6\u00f0 Ioseph: Ic hyne geseah on \u00feam ylcan fl\u00e6sce, \u00fee he \u00e6ror w\u00e6s, and his\n\u00c6fter\u00feam \u00fea \u00f0a Ioseph \u00feus gesprecen h\u00e6fde, \u00fea com \u00fe\u00e6t arwur\u00f0e wyf Veronix and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: \u00fe\u00e6t ic\nVolosianus het \u00fea Pilatum gefeccan and hym to cw\u00e6\u00f0: For hwig lete \u00feu ofslean godes sunu?\nPilatus hym andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hys agene \u00feeoda and \u00fea yldestan bisceopas hyne sealdon me.\nVolosianus \u00fea wear\u00f0 yrre geworden and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Swa me se sylfa dryhten lybbe, \u00feam wyrsestan\nAnd Volosianus hyne \u00fea eft het on \u00feam ysenan scryne gebryngan and on cwearterne gesettan and to\nVeronix hym \u00fea swy\u00f0e wy\u00f0soc and s\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t heo nane halignyssa myd hyre n\u00e6fde.\nAc Volosianus hyre na ne gelyfde, ac hig swa \u00feeah genydde myd myclum ege, \u00fe\u00e6t heo hyt ameldode\nVolosianus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Agif me \u00feone dryhten, \u00fee \u00f0u to geeadmeddest, and ic hyne wylle eac geeadmedan.\nVeronix \u00fea swa dyde and hym forwyrnan ne dorste.\nVolosianus, \u00fea seo halignis hym w\u00e6s to broht, \u00fea feoll he ny\u00f0er astreht and myd ryhtum geleafan\nAc hyt eallinga swa n\u00e6s, ac hyt w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t reaf, \u00fe\u00e6t se sylfa h\u00e6lend werede.\nAnd Volosianus \u00fea \u00f0a he up aras, he \u00feone andwlytan genam and swa wende, \u00fe\u00e6t hyt Crystes andwlita\nAnd \u00fea scytan he dyde \u00fea on an gylden f\u00e6t and hyt myd hys hringe geinseglode and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Swa\nAc ic wat, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea het Pilatum \u00feam fulestan dea\u00f0e acwylman and w\u00e6s hym sy\u00f0\u00f0an toweard hys\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t arwur\u00f0e wyf \u00fea Veronix ealle hyre \u00e6hta for Crystes naman forlet and w\u00e6s Volosiane\nAc Volosianus hyre to cw\u00e6\u00f0: La wyf, hw\u00e6t secest \u00feu?\nHeo hym andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic sece mynne dryhten, and la, hw\u00e6t h\u00e6bbe ic gedon, ic axie \u00fee, \u00fe\u00e6t\nTo so\u00f0on ic \u00fee secge, gif \u00feu hyne nelt me agyfan, ne forl\u00e6te ic n\u00e6fre \u00fee, \u00e6r\u00feon \u00f0e ic geseo, hwar \u00feu\n\u00dea \u00fe\u00e6t folc \u00fe\u00e6t gehyrde, hu Veronix \u00fe\u00e6t arwur\u00f0e wyf gespecen h\u00e6fde, hig sona ealle hyre\nAc Veronix heom to cw\u00e6\u00f0: La Hierusalemes bearn, ne wepon ge na ofer me, ac wepa\u00f0 ofer eow and\nVolosianus \u00fea het hys scypmen swy\u00f0e for\u00f0 rowan and \u00fe\u00e6r b\u00e6ftan let Titum and Vespasianum and\nAnd Tyberius \u00fea w\u00e6s swy\u00f0e geblyssigende and het Volosianum hym ra\u00f0e to cuman and hyne sona\nIc \u00fee bydde, gebycna hyt ealle me.\nVolosianus \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0: La myn hlaford, ealle \u00fea \u00f0yng, \u00fee ic \u00fe\u00e6r gemette, ealle ic gedo, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu hig nu\n\u00d0\u00e6t ys \u00e6rest, \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fe\u00e6r gemette Tytum and Vespasianum \u00feyne getrywestan undercyningas and \u00fe\u00e6r\nAnd ic gemette \u00fe\u00e6r \u00feone casere onhangen and Caiphan and Archelaus geh\u00e6nedne and Pilatum\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t ys eall, for\u00feam \u00f0e \u00fea Iudeas \u00feone h\u00e6lendan Cryst myd sperum and myd stengum and myd\nNu for\u00feon Titus and Vespasianus hig habba\u00f0 yfelum dea\u00f0e acwylmede and swy\u00f0e mycle m\u00e6nige of\nAnd \u00feyne twegen getrywan cnyhtas comon of Arimathia, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ron Ioseph and Nychodemus, and\nAnd he \u00fea se sylfa h\u00e6lend on \u00feam \u00feryddan d\u00e6ge of dea\u00f0e aras and hyne hys leorningcnyhtum \u00e6tywde\nAnd eac he f\u00e6la wundra worhte \u00e6r hys \u00ferowunge: he deade awehte and he blynde gelyhte and he\nAnd Titus and Vespasianus heom \u00fe\u00e6t wra\u00f0e forguldon, \u00fea \u00f0a hig \u00fea Iudeas ahengon \u00fea fet up and \u00fe\u00e6t\nSe h\u00e6lend w\u00e6s ofslagen butan \u00e6lcon gylte, and \u00fea Iudeas w\u00e6ron ofslagene \u00feam fulostan dea\u00f0e and\nAnd eac we \u00fe\u00e6r an wyf gemetton, seo s\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t heo dryhtnes andwlitan h\u00e6fde.\nNu h\u00e6bbe ic her, cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge \u00fe\u00e6t wyf and eac \u00feone andwlitan.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Tyberius: Eala, swy\u00f0e w\u00e6s ic gewylnigende, \u00fe\u00e6t ic hyne geseon wolde and hyne\nVolosianus \u00fea up astod and \u00feone p\u00e6ll astrehte, \u00fee dryhtnes andwlytan on w\u00e6s befealden, and\nAc hyt eallynga swa n\u00e6s, ac hyt w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t reaf, \u00fee se sylfa dryhten werede.\nAc \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00f0enra manna, \u00feonne he \u00e6rest on beseah, hym \u00feuhte, \u00fe\u00e6t hyt drihtnes andwlyta w\u00e6re.\nAnd Tiberius hyne sylfne geea\u00f0medde, and se hreofla, \u00fee hym \u00e6r lange on w\u00e6s, wear\u00f0 \u00fea sona ny\u00f0er\nAnd he sona gelyfde and wear\u00f0 gefullod and eall hys hyred and eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc, \u00fee hym underge\u00feeodd\n\u00deam sig wuldor and wur\u00f0mynt a in ealra worulda woruld, Amen.",
